shape theory.contact : theory.transformation-law {
  type: definition
  layer: 0
  """
// Definition 5.1 (Contact).
// Contact is the structural relationship through which character
// enters a transformation. Contact has structure (the geometry
// governing what enters and how) and character (the specific content
// carried at each moment). Contact is itself a shape: it persists
// across moments and satisfies the Laws of Coherence.
//
// Contact is the structure of reference. Reference is the character
// of contact: the specific content carried across the contact boundary
// into a transformation. Contact is the shape; reference is what the
// shape produces.
//
// Derives from: theory.transformation-law (contact is how C enters f)
  """
}
